Date: Sun, 21 Mar 2021 16:54:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 051/196] Fix bench-bitcoin bug in BlockToJsonVerbose
 benchmark. (#102)

62c2bc5 added the requirement to check LowS for verbose serialization of sigs, but we didn't fix the benchmarks.

Since we always enforce Low S, the signature printing (for the human readable script asm) needs to check if the signature has low S. For that, we need access to a secp256k1 verify context. ECCVerifyHandle sets this up for us in the constructor and tears it down again in the destructor.
---
 src/bench/rpc_blockchain.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/bench/rpc_blockchain.cpp b/src/bench/rpc_blockchain.cpp
index ebb6e45f2..a56bb9007 100644
--- a/src/bench/rpc_blockchain.cpp
+++ b/src/bench/rpc_blockchain.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <bench/bench.h>
 #include <bench/data.h>
 
+#include <pubkey.h>
 #include <rpc/blockchain.h>
 #include <streams.h>
 #include <validation.h>
@@ -12,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <univalue.h>
 
 static void BlockToJsonVerbose(benchmark::Bench &bench) {
+    const ECCVerifyHandle verify_handle;
     CDataStream stream(benchmark::data::block413567, SER_NETWORK,
                        PROTOCOL_VERSION);
     char a = '\0';
